WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.063
Here's what the whole migration is for.

2
00:00:02.063 --> 00:00:07.653
Every person, device, server and workload
is governed by attributes that are true,

3
00:00:07.653 --> 00:00:10.824
owned by exactly one
source, and read by policy.

4
00:00:10.824 --> 00:00:15.757
Joining, moving and leaving change
access with no ticket, every non-person

5
00:00:15.757 --> 00:00:20.850
identity has an owner and a managed
credential, and AD can finally be retired.

6
00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:25.598
The table is how you know you're there,
track by track: every account traced to HR,

7
00:00:25.598 --> 00:00:29.011
every device and server
targeted by its own attributes,

8
00:00:29.011 --> 00:00:32.275
every service account owned,
and a clean drift report.

9
00:00:32.275 --> 00:00:35.121
That's design guidance
on the books' own gates,

10
00:00:35.121 --> 00:00:38.812
and the last column names the
federal rule each one serves.

11
00:00:38.812 --> 00:00:40.100
So, which rules?
